Now that Turbo C++ 1.0 is out and includes VROOM memory manager, could
someone compile nethack with it and send binaries to net. (Means when the
latest patches are out.) Seems that team which created the PC overlay
manager are out of work..

(For you who don't know what I'm talking about: VROOM divides the executable
file into pieces of a couple of kilobytes and can swap them to disk or
EMS memory. Should work and be much faster than conventional overlays.)
